!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/vocabulary-sidecar.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  Formal shape of a vocabulary-layer sidecar (tests/vocabulary/**/*-expected.tn) -- see README.md's
  own "Vocabulary-layer vectors" section for the worked example this schema formalizes, and its own
  extensive prose on exactly what `value` means per atom family (host-representation-neutral: a
  plain decimal string for the exact/approximate numeric families, a hex string for the binary
  family and ipv6's raw bytes, a "numerator/denominator" string for rational, an RFC 3339 string for
  the temporal family, ...).

  value is typed here as a plain, optional text field -- a deliberate simplification, not a full
  per-atom-family shape: two families (complex, duration) actually write value as a small NESTED
  RECORD in real sidecars ({ real: "..." imaginary: "..." } / { period: "..." clock: "..." }), which
  a single text field can't capture. Loosening this further (e.g. one shape per atom family) is left
  for whenever this schema is actually wired onto real sidecars via !!schema -- see README.md's own
  note on that being tracked separately, not done in this pass.
  """
{
  @doc:"Shared across every layer's own sidecar schema (see README.md's 'Invalid vectors (any layer)' section) -- one of the spec's own four §8.1 diagnostic categories."
  error_category => !enum [lexer parser resolver validation]

  @doc:"Fields every layer's sidecar shares -- spec/description are always present, encoding only when the .tn file isn't plain UTF-8."
  sidecar_common => {
    spec: text
    description: text
    encoding: text?
  }

  vocabulary_outcome => !enum [valid error]

  vocabulary_sidecar => sidecar_common & {
    outcome: vocabulary_outcome
    type-ref: text?
    value: text?
    category: error_category?
  }
}
